/-!
# The relative dimension of the local model of an affine bundle

The structure morphism `Spec(B[z₁, z₂]/(z₁z₂ - f)) ⟶ Spec B` of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.AffineBundle.LocalModelMorphism` has **relative dimension
one**: every nonempty fibre is equidimensional of topological Krull dimension `1`.

By `Stacks.AffineBundle.baseChangeEquiv` the fibre over a prime `𝔭` of `B` is the local model
over the residue field `κ(𝔭)` of the image of `f` there, so everything reduces to the statement
that `K[z₁, z₂]/(z₁z₂ - c)` is one-dimensional and equidimensional for a field `K` and `c : K`.
Both halves of that are instances of a statement about an arbitrary hypersurface in a polynomial
ring over a field, proved here: the quotient by one nonzero nonunit is equidimensional, every
irreducible component having the dimension of the whole. No case distinction on `c` is needed,
and in particular the reducible fibre `K[z₁, z₂]/(z₁z₂)` over the vanishing locus of `f` is not
treated separately.

## Main results

* `Stacks.MvPolynomial.specEquidimensional_quotient_span_singleton` — **a hypersurface in affine
  space over a field is equidimensional**, each of its components having the dimension of the
  whole hypersurface.
* `Stacks.AffineBundle.ringKrullDim_localModel_field` and
  `Stacks.AffineBundle.equidimensional_primeSpectrum_localModel` — the local model over a field
  is equidimensional of Krull dimension one.
* `Stacks.AffineBundle.relativeDimension_localModelSpecMap` — **the structure morphism of the
  local model has relative dimension one.**

## Implementation notes

Equidimensionality is proved in the ring-theoretic spelling `SpecEquidimensional` of
`StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Equidimensional.FlatLocal`, which compares `ringKrullDim (R ⧸ 𝔭)` over
the minimal primes `𝔭` of `R`, and is turned into the topological
`TopologicalSpace.Equidimensional` by `specEquidimensional_iff_equidimensional`. For
`R = k[ι]/(z)` a minimal prime of `R` is the image of a prime of `k[ι]` minimal over `(z)`, by
`Ideal.mem_minimalPrimes_sup` applied with `J = ⊥`, and `Ideal.quotQuotEquivQuotOfLE` identifies
the two quotients. Such a prime has height one — at most one by Krull's principal ideal theorem,
and not zero because it contains the nonzero `z` while `k[ι]` is a domain — hence is itself
principal, `k[ι]` being a unique factorization domain; so
`Stacks.MvPolynomial.ringKrullDim_quotient_span_singleton`, which needs no hypothesis on the
quotient, computes its quotient dimension, and the answer does not depend on the component.

That the relation `z₁z₂ - f` is neither zero nor a unit is checked by evaluation: the coefficient
of `z₁z₂` is `1`, and the relation vanishes at `(1, f)`, so a unit would have the non-unit `0` as
its image under a ring map.

The fibre of the structure morphism is identified with `Spec` of the fibre ring by
`AlgebraicGeometry.fiberSpecHomeo`, and the fibre ring `κ(𝔭) ⊗_B B[z₁, z₂]/(z₁z₂ - f)` with the
local model over `κ(𝔭)` by `Stacks.AffineBundle.baseChangeEquiv`.

